{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Your reading study{% endblock %}
{% block extra_styles %}
  .study { padding: 24px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14px; }
  th, td { padding: 12px 6px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  caption { text-align: left; padding: 12px 0; }
{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<section class="card study">
  <a class="btn" href="/">Back to reading</a>
  <h1>Useful research picks per digest</h1>
  <p>This study uses your current explicit ratings from recent saved research slates. “Useful” means Relevant or Must read. Unrated papers remain unknown. Repeated papers can share a rating across days; this is not an independent comparison of ranking algorithms or proof of improvement.</p>
  <table><caption>Up to 14 recent digests · current ratings</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Digest</th><th scope="col">Useful</th><th scope="col">Rated</th><th scope="col">Unrated</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{% for day in days %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ day.digest_id }}</th><td>{{ day.useful }}</td><td>{{ day.rated }}</td><td>{{ day.unrated }}</td></tr>{% else %}<tr><td colspan="4">No saved research slates yet. Rate papers after your next brew to build this study.</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
  </table>
  <p>No missing ratings are counted as successes or failures. Legacy neutral votes without an explicit grade remain unknown. Historical slates without item membership cannot be evaluated here.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
